  "body": "Process change: yes\n\n## What changed\n\n- A Wire Contour has a new parameter, `compensation`: `computer` (the default, as before), `control` or `wear`.\n- The generator makes and judges the same wire-centre path as before. With `control` or `wear`, each pass then gets one `CompSpan` (`motion::wire_edm::wire_comp_spans`, a new module `comp.rs`).\n  - Control: the span's programmed geometry is the part contour. Each ring move moves back by the offset along its normal. A line moves by translation, an arc keeps its centre and changes its radius. Two lines at a mitred joint meet at the part corner. A corner round that the offset put in collapses to its corner.\n  - Wear: the programmed geometry is the wire-centre walk itself.\n  - Each span states its pass's kerf offset (wire radius plus the gap of the pass's condition) as its radius. The rough pass is first, then each skim.\n- The post dump already writes a span between `COMP` records (M13.11). So the LN2W post of #4139 writes `G41` / `G42 Hnnn` by pass, with `C001` and `H001` first, and `G40` on each lead-out. The post and the engine do not change.\n- The command door (`wire_gate`) and the generator refuse control or wear by name with: an open run, a 4-axis cut, a taper, a burnout, tabs, the arc lead, an exit pick (`operation::wire_comp::refusal`).\n- The span builder refuses by name: a lead-in or lead-out shorter than the pass's offset, an arc lead, a pass that does not return to the start hole, a hairpin turn, an arc at a sharp joint.\n- Mark 21, G-EDM and the other wire posts refuse the offset by name (their existing hooks, or the engine's refusal).\n- Project file: the key `compensation` is written only when it is not `computer`. The stamp digests it only then. No existing file or stamp changes.\n- MCP: the parameter rides the operation DTO, so `add_operation` and `edit_operation` take it. `list_operation_types` lists it. The `camcraft-mcp` skill row names it (a process file: `Process change: yes`).\n- Each `WireContourOp` literal in the tests gets `compensation: Default::default()`.\n\n## Cause\n\n`posting_wire.rs` posted only the wire-centre path, and the op had no mode. No LN2W program with the control's offset could come from the app (#4134).\n\n## Item 3 of the issue: how the wire laws judge the path\n\nThe kerf, threading and slug laws judge the wire-centre moves, as before. These moves are what the control cuts when each register holds the radius that its span states. The post writes that radius in the comment before each `G41` / `G42` line (`THE STREAM STATES 0.165 MM`). The decision is in `docs/decisions/4134-wire-control-offset.md`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all new):\n\n- `camcraft-motion` lib, `wire_edm::comp::tests` (9): `a_die_square_is_programmed_on_its_profile_under_g41`, `a_punch_square_is_programmed_on_its_profile_under_g42`, `a_reversed_skim_takes_the_other_side`, `each_pass_states_its_own_radius`, `the_wear_span_programs_the_wire_centre_moves`, `computer_compensation_records_nothing`, `a_circle_is_programmed_as_arcs_at_the_part_radius`, `a_lead_in_shorter_than_the_offset_is_refused_by_name`, `an_arc_lead_and_an_open_run_are_refused_by_name`.\n- `camcraft-app` `wire_post`, `sodick_aq600l::offset` (5): `the_ln2w_square_posts_the_part_contour_with_the_controls_offset`, `the_ln2w_two_axis_block_posts_the_part_arcs_with_the_controls_offset`, `the_ln2w_square_posts_the_wire_centre_path_with_a_wear_offset`, `the_mark_21_post_refuses_the_controls_offset_by_name`, `the_offset_with_a_taper_or_an_open_run_is_refused_at_the_door`.\n- `camcraft-app` lib, `the_wire_compensation_round_trips_and_is_absent_for_computer`.\n- `mcp_wire_contour::list_operation_types_and_skill_match_wire_contour_dto_and_tool_law` now includes `compensation`.\n\nRed before the fix: the pins do not compile on `upstream/main` (no `compensation` field, no `wire_comp_spans`).\n\nMutations (each run, then restored, then green):\n\n- Generation hook removed (`generate.rs` from `upstream/main`): 4 of 5 `offset` pins red (the door pin stays green, as it must).\n- Door refusal removed (`gates.rs`): `the_offset_with_a_taper_or_an_open_run_is_refused_at_the_door` red.\n- Corner mitre replaced by the single normal (`comp.rs`): the die and the punch square pins red.\n- Lead-length law disabled (`comp.rs`): `a_lead_in_shorter_than_the_offset_is_refused_by_name` red.\n\nGate on the final head: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` on head a8a162041952d7216a8f402a465fba5743a3ea73: 779 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled (49.7 min). It ran every app suite (the new golden is a shared test input), `motion suites: lib`, the post script suites and `example_catalog` / `example_catalog_adaptive` / `example_catalog_edge_work`.\n\nClippy: `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`, the same for `camcraft-app` and `camcraft-ui`: clean on the final head.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\n- New: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-ln2w/edm_test_square_offset.nc` (rough C001 and skims C002, C903; `G41 H001` / `H002` / `H003`; the part square at X5. Y5.; `G40 G01 X0. Y0.` on each lead-out).\n- New: `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/sodick-ln2w/edm_test_2axis_offset.nc` (the holes at the part radii 2.5 mm and 3 mm, the slot edges at Y-2.8 and Y-3.2).\n- Changed: none. The existing LN2W, Mark 21 and other wire goldens stay byte-identical (no tracked golden is in the diff).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No physical LN2W control. The words are the owner's rules from #4076.\n- Control mode on a drawn DXF line-and-arc chain is wired (the same hook after `generate_arcs`), but no golden pins it.\n- The UI has no control for the mode yet: #4243 (two open PRs change `wire_page.rs`).\n- Heavy lanes: not run (P6; AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\": no PR gets the full heavy lanes).\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- #3617 (contributor, `needs-rework`) adds the `overlap` field to the same structs and literals (`WireContourOp`, the DTO, the seed, `list_operation_types`, `create.rs`) and changes `announce_skims`. This PR does not change `announce_skims`. It adds its lines after `lead_arc_radius`, away from the lines of #3617. Not stacked: the overlap is \"both sides added lines\", and a stack would hold this feature on another author's rework. Whichever merges second refreshes. The decision record says why.\n\nChangelog: Wire Contour: a compensation mode (computer, control, wear). With control, the Sodick LN2W post writes the part contour under G41/G42 Hnnn (one register for each pass, from H001) with G40 on each lead-out; the wire laws still judge the wire-centre path.\n\nFixes #4134\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
